  "notes": "{越|こ}す means to cross over, move past, or exceed something.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nCan be both transitive and intransitive depending on usage.\n\nTHREE MAIN MEANINGS:\n1. To cross/pass over: {山|やま}を{越|こ}す (cross a mountain)\n2. To move residence: {新|あたら}しい{家|いえ}に{越|こ}す\n3. To exceed: {予算|よさん}を{越|こ}す (exceed the budget)\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n- {引|ひ}っ{越|こ}す: to move (residence)\n- {乗|の}り{越|こ}す: to ride past one's stop\n- {追|お}い{越|こ}す: to overtake, pass by\n- {年|とし}を{越|こ}す: to see the New Year in\n\nCONTRAST WITH {超|こ}える:\nBoth mean \"to exceed,\" but {越|こ}す emphasizes physical crossing while {超|こ}える emphasizes surpassing limits.",
